    {
      "id": "claim_6d6b80b5c1e54f04a6ae3ab54a0f4e5d",
      "statement": "The non-default-app fallback runs through SmsContentObserver (registered by the ViewModels on BOTH Telephony.Sms and Telephony.Mms URIs, firing on the main looper, leading-edge immediate dispatch with 150 ms coalescing whose trailing call passes null) into ChangeRouter, which routes URIs with an extractable row id — source table chosen by URI authority, not path substring — to a targeted O(1) Upsert/Delete mutation on Dispatchers.IO, and id-less or null URIs to a reconcile downgraded to ForThread when LocalProviderWrites claims a recent mark-read, otherwise FullSync; row-id URIs are treated as an optimization, not a contract, because Android does not guarantee them on all OEM builds.",
      "evidence": [
