    {
      "id": "claim_700f5a5e459c444188e5acb776818d66",
      "statement": "WebhookEngine.sendIncomingSmsWebhook gates both legs on GatewayAccessPolicy.canTransmit (versioned gateway consent AND the supervisor-derived runtime isEnabled flag), skipping everything when it fails; when open it fires two fire-and-forget IO coroutines — an HTTPS-only local webhook POST (non-HTTPS rejected; optional HMAC-SHA256 X-Signature over '<timestamp>.<body>' with X-Timestamp; 8 s timeouts) and a cloud event to /api/gateways/events/sms (only when registered with a token) whose deterministic name-based eventId is checked against a local sent-event cache and marked sent only on Success; failures are logged and never thrown into the receiver.",
      "evidence": [
